nodecode-foundry is a rewrite of dolepee's dolepee/hermes-plugin-foundry:

  https://github.com/dolepee/hermes-plugin-foundry
  commit 9345a56954d219f923a05712a7a68e44df5099a2
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Iyanda Abdulqodir Adedolapo (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the one sentence a request is read as (a folder to watch or a URL to poll, one
file type, an interval in minutes, a name and a slug from what it names), the two
archetypes with their state of what has already been reported, the one root every write
lands under with symlinks followed and a path outside it refused, the static scan over the
generated text, and the five verbs — plan, build, test, list, catalog — as tools and as
one slash command. The state is a text file of names rather than SQLite, a database being
a dependency a cell does not need for a list of names it already reported; the check is the
reader run with evaluation off plus the scan, rather than a test subprocess, because
nothing generated is executed here at all.

Left out: the Hermes manifest and plugin surface (`plugin.yaml`, `__init__.py`, the
`pre_tool_call` and `post_approval_response` hooks and the tool-execution middleware),
which a cell does not have — the root is the fence, so a path outside it refuses in words
instead of asking for an approval — and the printed list of files it generates for a
Hermes plugin, since a cell's folder is not a manifest. Also left out: the request reader's
longer sentence-archetype table for suffix punctuation and output-purpose clauses; a
request here names one file type or refuses, which is the same fail-closed posture with a
smaller rule.
